    "bubble_choice_description": "The Painter’s paint supply almost — but not quite — matches this path. Help it paint as far as it can before the paint runs out.",
    "display_name": "Close Call",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Coding Tip:** This board is built so the obstacle and the paint supply almost match — but not quite. If you compare your fixed code against the starter code, the Painter should stop a few squares earlier once `has_paint()` is added, instead of running all the way to the wall with a paint error message in the console along the way.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/2f67bfb6e0af8ddd7ff781361599d5bc-Screenshot 2026-11-04 101807.png",
    "validation_file": {
      "id": "2",
      "name": "test.py",
      "contents": "import ast\nfrom unittest import TestCase\nfrom unittest_runner import ValidationProtocol\n\n\nclass TestModifyAddHasPaint(TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        \"\"\"Run the student's code and parse its structure\"\"\"\n        cls.log = ValidationProtocol().get_neighborhood_log()\n        cls.painter = cls.log.painter_logs[0] if cls.log.painter_logs else None\n        with open(\"main.py\") as f:\n            cls.source = f.read()\n        cls.tree = ast.parse(cls.source)\n        cls.while_nodes = [n for n in ast.walk(cls.tree) if isinstance(n, ast.While)]\n\n    def setUp(self):\n        if self.painter is None:\n            self.skipTest(\"No painter actions found yet. Make sure your program runs without errors.\")\n\n    def _calls_named(self, node, name):\n        \"\"\"True if name(...) is called anywhere inside node\"\"\"\n        return any(\n            isinstance(n, ast.Call) and isinstance(n.func, ast.Name) and n.func.id == name\n            for n in ast.walk(node)\n        )\n\n    def test_paint_loops_check_has_paint(self):\n        \"\"\"Both while loops stop as soon as can_move() or has_paint() is False\"\"\"\n        paint_loops = [n for n in self.while_nodes if self._calls_named(n.test, \"can_move\")]\n        self.assertEqual(\n            len(paint_loops),\n            2,\n            f\"Expected to find 2 while loops checking can_move(), but found {len(paint_loops)}. Make sure you didn't remove or combine either loop.\"\n        )\n        for loop in paint_loops:\n            condition = loop.test\n            is_and_combo = (\n                isinstance(condition, ast.BoolOp)\n                and isinstance(condition.op, ast.And)\n                and self._calls_named(condition, \"can_move\")\n                and self._calls_named(condition, \"has_paint\")\n            )\n            self.assertTrue(\n                is_and_combo,\n                \"Each while loop's condition should check can_move() and has_paint() together, like `while can_move() and has_paint():`. We found a loop still checking only one of them, or combining them with `or` instead of `and`.\"\n            )\n        self.assertGreater(\n            self.painter.action_count(\"HAS_PAINT\"),\n            0,\n            \"has_paint() didn't actually get called when we ran your program. Make sure it's part of the while condition, not just written somewhere else.\"\n        )",
      "folderId": "0",
      "active": false,
      "type": "validation"
    }
